{"t": 167.125, "n": 97, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Phase 5 is finished: the new `test_pause_hand_on.py` passes, and the plan marks for rows 5.3 and 5.4 are written. Only the final reply is left.\n\nRows 5.1, 5.2 and 5.5 already had marks from an earlier visit, so I left them alone. Row 5.4's code (`held_by_tickets`, the `held` flag, recorded-answer reuse) was already in `child.py`. I wrote only the 5.3 test file and marked both rows.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran `test_pause_hand_on.py` (10 passed), `test_stop_at_pause.py` and `test_pause_findings_at_final_exit.py` (all passed together with it, 39 tests); ruff on the new file found one unused variable, which I removed, and I did not re-run ruff after that. Built row 5.3 (new `test_pause_hand_on.py`, SIL-AC57/58/59 and AC 3) and marked 5.3 and 5.4 in one edit. Row 5.4's code was already in `child.py` from an earlier visit, so the test file came after its source, which may matter for SRC-B6, and I made no source change. Two deviations in the tests: a stopped thread re-opens with `retry` (not `proceed`) with the stand-in's steps reset, and the fixture thread has a second pause finding, so assertions are scoped to the `gap_escalation` fingerprint instead of counting all prompts or findings. The held-child test asserts at most one issue, not exactly one.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "7bfb09aa-481e-484c-adbf-888d4964ee97"}
